WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Imagine you are created in
mid-air, senses cut off,

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.280
touching nothing at all.

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.700
Would you still know that you exist?

4
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.900
Ibn Sina said yes.

5
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:16.420
From the 9th century, Greek philosophy
was translated into Arabic in Baghdad.

6
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.210
Muslim thinkers used
it to argue about God,

7
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.460
the soul and the resurrection.

8
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.680
So did philosophy help
faith, or put it to the test?

9
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.690
In this mission, you'll follow arguments
for God that later reached Thomas Aquinas.

10
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.640
Then you'll see how to speak of a
God the Qur'an says has no likeness.

11
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: weigh up whether
philosophy helped Muslim faith,

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.520
or tested it.
